infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The full-reload tax: client navigation vs crossing root layouts
  desc Same app, two navigation modes — patch the tree below a shared layout, or replace the whole document
  compares
    - label Client navigation (same root layout)
      children
        - label ~100 ms transition
          desc Router patches the tree below the shared layout
        - label Client state preserved
          desc Context, caches, open toast, half-typed form all survive
        - label No network round-trip
          desc Soft navigation, no full hydration
        - label Crossed ~40 times a day
          desc Dashboard to settings — keep this pair in one shell
    - label Full document reload (across root layouts)
      children
        - label ~0.5-1.5 s on mid-tier mobile
          desc Network round-trip plus full hydration
        - label All client state dies
          desc Context, caches, open toast gone with the document
        - label Nothing shared to patch
          desc html and body differ, so Next replaces the document
        - label Crossed once at login
          desc Marketing to app — the rare seam where the tax is fine
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
